{
  "addendum": "The Stage-8 additions and direct game comparator S37-S42 were each verified in Crossref, OpenAlex, and Semantic Scholar. On 2026-08-28 the three repair-precedent references added with the guided-repair method (S44-S46) were verified live against arXiv and OpenAlex (title and year matched on both); Semantic Scholar returned HTTP 429 for all three and is recorded as rate-limited, not as a match failure. On 2026-09-02 a top-venue refresh added S47-S51 (ASPLOS 2006, NeurIPS 2023, ACM Computing Surveys 1983, ICML 2024, CoRL 2022) and resolved S45 to its NeurIPS 2023 proceedings DOI; Crossref/OpenAlex answered, PMLR HTML metadata confirmed the two PMLR volumes, Semantic Scholar returned HTTP 429 for every lookup and is recorded as rate-limited, and OpenReview could not be queried for S46, which therefore stays PREPRINT. On 2026-09-02 a related-work refresh added S52-S56 (AgentSpec, Setting the DC, STORY2GAME, Beyond State Consistency, AgentRR) from the paper-framing feedback: the four arXiv preprints matched title, authors, and year on the arXiv API and OpenAlex (three of them only through arXiv-DOI lookup because OpenAlex title search returned unrelated records); Setting the DC is a non-archival NeurIPS 2025 GenProCC workshop paper whose OpenReview forum and API returned a browser challenge (HTTP 403) that was not bypassed, so its identity rests on the official NeurIPS 2025 virtual program record and the GenProCC accepted-paper list, which agree on title, five authors, and author order (Li, Zeng, Xi, Zhu, Ammanabrolu). Semantic Scholar returned HTTP 429 for all five and is recorded as rate-limited.",
